WEBVTT

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:09.750
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:20.280
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.470
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:06.950
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:14.220
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:20.960
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:28.390
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:31.580
As planned…

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:34.210
…with communication cables
intact, Chor Tempest…

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:36.080
…will descend as low as possible…

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.900
…and protect the Ruins from attack
by the Shoukoku-highland forces.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.330
The enemy?

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:55.340
<b>The Funeral</b>

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:05.350
This sibylla’s spirit is
bound by chains of sin.

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:10.180
Nevertheless, both the merciful
Tempus Spatium, as well as Kyuukoku…

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:12.830
…are prepared to
forgive and accept her.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.960
But why the heck was Anglas lying
dead inside an ancient Simoun?

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.340
That day, there’s no
question that she…

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.230
Aer!

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:55.650
They never found so much as
a bone fragment in the debris.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:07.950
This sibylla has just received
the divine grace of Tempus Spatium.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:11.290
Now that she is about to set off
on a new journey, let us pray.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.190
She was a highland priestess.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.870
Not only that, but a spy.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:45.100
How can we hold a funeral
for her on the Arcus Prima?

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.200
The high priestess felt it
was the right thing to do.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.700
And how did the
military council feel?

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:52.320
That since the Highlands and
Shoukoku are now allies…

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.250
…it wouldn’t do to send
even the remains back to them.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.750
And yet they’re so full
of mutual animosity.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:00.810
Yes, it seems they do agree
on the most unlikely thing.

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.740
And that’s what
causes trouble for us.

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:18.980
You won’t get a
breeze sitting here.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:23.240
Neviril.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:27.240
To think that you’d start a
conversation with me… Who knew?

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.250
What happened at the Ruins…

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.250
Yeah.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.070
Huh?

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:45.050
What?

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:49.050
The Spring.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.690
We found the Spring
inside the Ruins.

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:58.530
And Onasia was there.

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:01.460
This is…

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.800
…the Spring itself.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:06.450
It’s just like Grandpa said!

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:15.770
And then we found Anglas, who
surely perished in that explosion…

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:17.480
…inside an ancient Simoun.

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:21.410
I’m thinking that Anglas
went there herself.

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:22.430
What?

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:23.610
In that moment…

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:25.510
…the moment the Simoun exploded…

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.510
…she went to a different world.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:29.720
A different…

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:31.510
…world?

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:36.890
Just when we thought we were
back home on the Arcus Prima…

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:39.190
…all these weird
things started happening!

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:41.520
At least give us a
little downtime, right?

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.260
There’s no time to get comfortable.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:48.070
We’re to go to the maju
pool right after this.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.420
I do like majus…

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.700
…but not if we’re
being ordered to do them!

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.040
Wait, isn’t that Neviril
and Aer over there?

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:01.630
Hey, so they managed to make up!

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:03.250
What do you mean, make up?

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.550
Neviril was just having
a hissy fit on her own!

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:22.190
W-Wait, Aer. What do you mean by…

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:26.020
It’s something Grandpa told me once.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.700
Hey, hurry up! This way!

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:36.920
Grandpa, come on! Hurry!

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:38.030
Aer!

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:41.290
This is as far as I can go.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:42.320
Huh?

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:44.330
You go on ahead.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:48.840
Getting old means making
more and more choices.

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:52.430
And with every choice you make…

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:55.760
…you erase all
other possibilities.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:57.290
But I don’t understand!

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:01.310
The Simoun will show
you where you’re headed.

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:03.810
Where I’m headed?

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:08.690
To a different world!

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:15.020
What my grandpa meant by
that, I still don’t know.

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:17.870
But Grandpa was
always yearning for it.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:21.970
Aer, is that why you never
wanted to choose your gender?

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:27.840
The helical motors…

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:31.150
Said to manipulate
both time and space…

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:34.540
I thought it was
no more than a story…

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:36.990
…to strengthen the
mystery of the Simouns.

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:39.380
“Everywhere…

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:40.850
…and yet nowhere.”

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:44.900
If that’s true of Onasia…

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:47.340
…and true of Anglas…

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.360
…and true of the Simouns…

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:52.320
Then maybe…

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:53.910
…it’s true of Rimone
and Dominüra as well.

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:01.800
What we just talked about…

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:03.870
Let’s keep it between ourselves.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:05.420
So we’re going to share a secret!

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:08.340
Just the two of us!

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:11.340
Yes, we are.

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:18.550
Why didn’t you attend
Anglas’s funeral?

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:19.600
Those are the rules.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.590
A priestess from a
lowly family like mine…

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:24.600
…has no right to
attend a holy ceremony.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.060
B-But why?

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:28.380
— You joined us the other time.
— Things are different now.

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:30.430
Our leaders are in turmoil.

00:08:30.430 --> 00:08:33.610
But they allowed an enemy
priestess’s funeral to be held here.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.530
You don’t sound
like yourself at all.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:38.620
I thought you
liked that Anglas girl.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:41.190
But…

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:42.120
But…

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:47.130
I knew I’d have to face at least
this level of discrimination.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.370
What?

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:51.520
The only reason I got to the rank
of Simoun sibylla was because…

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:54.400
…I had the backing
of the vice chancellor.

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:56.030
Mamina.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:59.140
But the vice chancellor has changed.

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:04.140
He’s nothing but a
senile old geezer now.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:06.260
W-Wait a minute, Mamina!

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:09.870
I enjoyed our time on the Messis,
especially that mouse stew I made.

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:10.600
Huh?

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:13.340
Watching all you oh-so-noble
priestesses taste that stew…

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:16.140
…I thought, “Hey, they’re
just the same as me!”

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:17.560
That’s right. We’re the same!

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:20.970
Nope.

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:22.460
We’re not the same after all.

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:30.250
Mamina…

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:37.130
Please wait a moment.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:40.100
The maju pool is under the
jurisdiction of the chancellors.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:42.830
Should you set foot in this area…

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:44.420
— …the high priestess will…
— It doesn’t matter.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:00.230
Military Councilor.

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:02.850
You must forgive us…

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:05.260
…but we can’t have
so many observers.

00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:07.210
It will disturb our prayers.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.090
A maju is not a prayer.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:12.920
It is battle practice,
Sibylla Aurea.

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:16.750
I’d like to see for myself.

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:20.070
What Chor Tempest is
currently capable of…

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:22.930
The Ri Majon with the
most destructive power!

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:42.450
What a lovely wake
they’re creating.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:47.740
The Dandelion Ri Majon?

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:50.460
The one that harms no one…

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:52.690
…that leads no one astray…

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:54.840
…the one for ceremonies…

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:11.100
It’s better this way.

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:14.200
I didn’t make the
wrong choice after all.

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:18.570
Entrusting Aer to
become Neviril’s pair…

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:22.320
Yes, it’s all good
because of that.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:25.490
You have no clue whatsoever!

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:29.440
Could the judgment of
someone who’s been asleep…

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:31.990
…be less questionable
than your own?

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:35.180
Thinking someone
like you can protect her…

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:36.500
…is gross arrogance.

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:40.510
I…

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:41.550
…let Neviril…

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:45.890
I think…

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:48.340
…I might have made a mistake.

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:53.400
With you…

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.690
Don’t say it.

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:00.860
I think…

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:02.820
…I might have made a mistake.

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:09.910
I want to pair up with you.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:12.080
Yes.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:15.250
After all, I’m the one who
should be protecting you.

00:12:49.340 --> 00:12:51.570
Dismantle a Simoun…

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:57.200
I never thought I’d hear those
words from anyone else but you…

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:58.500
…Sibylla Dominüra.

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:03.080
Forget about that day, Waporif.

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:08.470
That’s the last warning
I’ll be giving you.

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:12.270
But how could I ever forget?

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:14.510
“Without something to believe in…

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:17.020
…none of us can even
plant our feet on the earth.”

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:18.630
That’s what you told me.

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:21.370
Have you found
something to believe in?

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:25.490
What am I supposed to do now?

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:35.330
What should I believe in?

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:51.150
I have ordered
the maintenance crew…

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:53.680
…to dismantle the ancient
Simoun as you instructed.

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:57.730
Dismantling a divine vessel.
How sacrilegious.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:59.720
Which is more sacrilegious?

00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:03.440
Allowing our holy Tempus Spatium
to be tainted by outsiders?

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:07.200
The topic for discussion today…

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:10.450
…is what to do about
that enemy air base.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:14.540
As most of the ancient Simouns
are now in the enemy’s hands…

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:16.940
…I believe it would be
dangerous to send Chor Tempest…

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:20.380
— …out on a reconnaissance mission…
— Then when would you deem it safe?

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:24.280
I understand your concern for
your daughter’s well-being.

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:26.880
However, should another
incident occur…

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:31.340
…next time for sure, you won’t have
a leg to stand on, Vice Chancellor.

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:35.310
Who is paired up with Sibylla Neviril?

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:37.140
That would be Sibylla Aer.

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:40.160
Out of all the members
of Chor Tempest…

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:42.560
…she has no parallel
as an auriga.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:44.400
Sibylla Aer?

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:46.280
If I recall, her grandfather was…

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:49.780
Even so, she herself…

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:51.780
What is the meaning of this?

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.780
Oh, please forgive me.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:03.750
Where are you taking her?

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:04.930
Sibylla Yun.

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:07.450
Anglas’s funeral is long over.

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:10.330
Shouldn’t she have been committed
to the earth as soon as possible?

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:12.720
This is an order from
the military councilor.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:14.340
The military councilor?

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:18.730
How dare you debase a departed
spirit. I won’t allow this to happen!

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:33.530
Once you’ve left the cockpit of a
Simoun, a woman is utterly powerless.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:47.160
It would be too
dangerous to sit back…

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:49.970
…and do nothing about
that mobile air base.

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:54.170
We are hereby sending Chor Tempest
on a reconnaissance mission.

00:15:54.170 --> 00:15:56.540
The Messis shall serve
as the relay point…

00:15:56.540 --> 00:16:00.480
What? Just when we finally got away
from that musty, old rust bucket!

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:03.480
I am happy to welcome
you all back, Sibyllae!

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:07.520
And if we discover the base?

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:09.950
That will be left to
your discretion, but…

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:10.740
As for me…

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:15.240
…I do believe you have the
capacity to blow it up at this point.

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:20.530
As both Sibylla Dominüra and Sibylla
Rimone are missing in action…

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:23.490
…we will have to
readjust your pairings.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:27.460
Sibylla Paraietta and Sibylla Kaim.

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:31.920
Sibylla Alty and Sibylla Floe.

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:34.930
Sibylla Roatreamon and Sibylla Morinas.

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:36.680
Sibylla Neviril…

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:39.130
…and Sibylla Mamina.

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:42.890
Sibylla Yun and Sibylla Aer…

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:47.440
It’s been decided that you two will
sit out this particular mission.

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:51.650
What are you talking about?
Why am I being left behind?

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:55.850
Aer is my pair.

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:58.580
You’ll have to convince me as well!

00:17:02.090 --> 00:17:03.540
Neviril…

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:07.080
Please, don’t cause
any more trouble for me.

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:26.560
What’s the matter?
You can’t sleep, Neviril?

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:27.690
No.

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:31.290
Your maju this afternoon.
It was magnificent.

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:33.320
Thank you.

00:17:37.960 --> 00:17:40.200
How about… a dance?

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:43.100
I’m sorry. I’m not in the mood.

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:49.210
What?

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:08.330
I never thought you’d
stand up for Aer.

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:11.560
It’s not that I’ve opened
up to her completely.

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:14.750
But by coming face
to face with Aer…

00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:16.650
…I’m also coming face
to face with Amuria…

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:19.570
…meaning I’m facing
up to myself as well.

00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:25.670
That may have been my
greatest fear all this time.

00:18:28.510 --> 00:18:30.920
And I was just trying to avoid it.

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:34.480
I’ve allowed you all to
humor me far too long.

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:36.980
So let me humor you.

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:40.930
Paraietta.

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:43.930
You can go ahead
and lean on me.

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:48.410
But at this rate…

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:49.980
…I won’t make it to a different world.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:52.940
Nothing, never mind
what I just said.

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:01.370
A different world, you say?

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:04.760
If it’s a different
world you long for…

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:06.290
…then I’ll show you one now!

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:08.410
Parai…

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:01.800
What is it?

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:03.470
You’re awake?

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:05.430
Yun’s fast asleep, I think.

00:20:06.110 --> 00:20:09.520
I just thought you might
be too nervous to sleep.

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:12.030
Pairing up with Sibylla Aurea…

00:20:12.030 --> 00:20:17.180
…I always saw that as the
fastest way to achieve my goals.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.250
Right.

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:20.770
But I don’t want you
to get the wrong idea.

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:25.240
Deep down, I do want the rest
of you to see me as an equal.

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:26.240
But…

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:28.030
…not for the same
reasons as before.

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:30.540
It’s because…

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:35.040
…I really want to be
friends with you all.

00:20:39.110 --> 00:20:40.550
Mamina…

00:20:41.350 --> 00:20:43.560
So stop saying things like,
“We’re friends,” will you?

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:45.670
It’s just a matter of
how you feel about me.

00:20:47.150 --> 00:20:48.550
Okay.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:53.350
Mamina, do you want me
to sing you a lullaby?

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:56.290
You mean the one
you sang for Rimone?

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:59.070
Give me a break!
I’m not a child.

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:05.080
<i>Hear the echo…</i>

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:07.070
Sorry, not listening.

00:21:06.340 --> 00:21:12.000
<i>…of the swirling light…</i>

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:24.650
<i>…bringing us tales of joy.</i>

00:21:28.090 --> 00:21:36.450
<i>Proof that an
eternal world exists…</i>

00:21:36.450 --> 00:21:43.190
<i>…shall be revealed
by Tempus Spatium.</i>

00:21:43.810 --> 00:21:51.530
<i>Rocking gently until
we awake tomorrow…</i>

00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:48.480
Why do you think they
took you off the mission?

00:21:48.480 --> 00:21:50.490
I have a pretty good idea.

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:51.530
You do, huh?

00:21:51.530 --> 00:21:52.700
What about you?

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:54.250
There’s something that bothers me.

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:55.290
What’s that?

00:21:56.350 --> 00:21:57.790
I can’t tell you…

00:21:57.790 --> 00:21:59.290
…because I promised not to.

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:00.960
I see.

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:02.430
That’s wise of you.

00:22:03.190 --> 00:22:06.800
Promises are made
to be kept after all.

00:22:19.710 --> 00:22:22.270
I’ve got to go now.

00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:23.440
As do I.

00:22:41.060 --> 00:22:47.780
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.780 --> 00:22:52.020
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.020 --> 00:22:59.090
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.090 --> 00:23:06.680
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:19.570
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.570 --> 00:23:24.750
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:28.720
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:32.760
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:38.630
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.630 --> 00:23:44.170
<i>Soar away into the
sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.170 --> 00:23:47.610
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:53.270
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.270 --> 00:23:59.500
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.710
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:06.380 --> 00:24:08.670
Neviril’s Simoun is shot down…

00:24:08.670 --> 00:24:13.090
…and forced to make an emergency
landing on Shoukoku’s aerial base.

00:24:14.060 --> 00:24:15.550
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:20.020
<b>Sibylla</b>

00:24:16.390 --> 00:24:17.510
Sibylla.
